WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:13.789
Enrollment is for bringing many devices into your fleet without
registering them one at a time. Reserve their names and serial
numbers before they leave the factory, then let each device
claim its own record when it first connects.

2
00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:27.768
First, create a batch policy. The quota limits how many devices
may enroll, and the lifetime limits how long the policy can be
used. These controls help keep a provisioning batch from
remaining open indefinitely.

3
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:42.155
Paste the names and serial numbers from your roster, then choose
Check. This lets you review the inventory before registering
claims. Consistent names make the devices easier to identify
once they appear in the fleet.

4
00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:56.619
Download the credentials and keep the exported file private.
During provisioning, give each unit only its own claim
credential. Do not put the whole credential file into a shared
device image or source repository.

5
00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:14.173
Register the pending claims and approve the requests. A claim
reserves an enrollment opportunity; it does not mean a device is
online yet. At first boot, each configured client uses its
credential to enroll. Watch for the record to move from waiting
to enrolled.

